。\\n     7\\t- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\\n     8\\t\\n     9\\t参考题目如下：\\n    10\\t<reference_puzzle index=\\\"1\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"8a6d367c\\\" lines=\\\"52-67\\\">\\n    11\\t<description>\\n    12\\tComplete the framed area by expanding the unique upper template that contains the existing seed pixels.\\n    13\\t\\n    14\\tInput structure:\\n    15\\t- A teal background contains small colored template masks above a larger rectangular frame.\\n    16\\t- The frame encloses one fill color arranged as a partial block-scaled copy of one template.\\n    17\\t- The frame interior dimensions are an integer square scale of the matching template bbox.\\n    18\\t\\n    19\\tRule:\\n    20\\t- Crop to the rectangular frame.\\n    21\\t- Identify the unique upper template whose block-scaled mask covers every existing fill pixel inside the frame.\\n    22\\t- Reset the frame interior to background and paint the whole scaled mask with the fill color.\\n    23\\t\\n    24\\tKey insight:\\n    25\\tThe lower colored pixels are seed cells that reveal which upper template should be completed inside the frame.\\n    26\\t</description>\\n    27\\t</reference_puzzle>\\n    28\\t\\n    29\\t<reference_puzzle index=\\\"2\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"cf5fd0ad\\\" lines=\\\"10-22\\\">\\n    30\\t<description>\\n    31\\tBuild a four-quadrant rotational tiling of the input square.\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\tInput structure\\n    34\\t- The input is a square grid treated as one complete sprite.\\n    35\\t\\n    36\\tRule\\n    37\\t- Each output quadrant is a 2x2 repetition of a rotated copy of the whole input.\\n    38\\t- The quadrant rotations are upper-left 180 degrees, upper-right 90 degrees\\n    39\\t  clockwise, lower-left 90 degrees counterclockwise, and lower-right unchanged.\\n    40\\t\\n    41\\tKey insight\\n    42\\t- The output is a 4x4 grid of original-size blocks, not a per-pixel scale-up.\\n    43\\t</description>\\n    44\\t</reference_puzzle>\\n    45\\t\\n    46\\t<reference_puzzle index=\\\"3\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"a6f40cea\\\" lines=\\\"74-88\\\">\\n    47\\t<description>\\n    48\\tComplete partial paths inside a framed rectangle by projecting external color traces inward.\\n    49\\t\\n    50\\tInput structure:\\n    51\\t- bg, a 1px rectangular frame (border color) with uniform interior fill.\\n    52\\t- Colored components outside the frame touching its edges.\\n    53\\t\\n    54\\tRule:\\n    55\\t- Output = the frame's interior, filled with the fill color.\\n    56\\t- Map each outside component's frame-touch points into interior coordinates.\\n    57\\t- Monochrome components become solid Manhattan stripes between mapped endpoints.\\n    58\\t- Two-color components become alternating-color Manhattan paths.\\n    59\\t\\n    60\\tKey insight: Endpoint colors of two-color traces anchor the alternating phase deterministically.\\n    61\\t</description>\\n    62\\t</reference_puzzle>\\n    63\\t\\n    64\\t<reference_puzzle index=\\\"4\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"2ccd9fef\\\" lines=\\\"173-187\\\">\\n    65\\t<description>\\n    66\\tPredict the next panel in a framed sequence by continuing each scheduled colored interval.\\n    67\\t\\n    68\\tInput structure\\n    69\\t- The grid is made from three or more equal panels in one row or one column.\\n    70\\t- The final input panel is the static target template; every earlier panel differs from it only by dynamic colors absent from the template.\\n    71\\t- Each dynamic color appears in a regular temporal schedule across the earlier panels.\\n    72\\t\\n    73\\tRule\\n    74\\t- Keep the final template panel as the output canvas.\\n    75\\t- For every dynamic color whose schedule reaches the next panel, compare its last two appearances.\\n    76\\t- Extrapolate each one-dimensional interval along the color's changing row or column axis and paint that predicted mask.\\n    77\\t\\n    78\\tKey insight\\n    79\\t- The task is not asking for the last visible panel, but for the next frame after the blank/template slot.\\n    80\\t</description>\\n    81\\t</reference_puzzle>\\n    82\\t\\n    83\\t<reference_puzzle index=\\\"5\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"ecb67b6d\\\" lines=\\\"138-155\\\">\\n    84\\t<description>\\n    85\\tRecolor the grey diagonal-chain regions in an orange field to teal.\\n    86\\t\\n    87\\tInput structure\\n    88\\tThe input contains only grey pixels and orange pixels.  Grey pixels form\\n    89\\tseveral 8-connected regions embedded in the orange field.\\n    90\\t\\n    91\\tRule\\n    92\\tDecompose each grey 8-connected region into 4-connected lobes.  Recolor the\\n    93\\twhole region teal only when it contains a straight diagonal run of at least\\n    94\\tthree pixels and those lobes meet only by diagonal corner contacts in a\\n    95\\tnon-branching diagonal chain or cycle; a single 4-connected region is\\n    96\\trecolored only when it is a square diagonal staircase.\\n    97\\t\\n    98\\tKey insight\\n    99\\tThe teal regions are not selected by size or position; they are the grey\\n   100\\tregions whose internal connectivity depends on diagonal corner joins, while\\n   101\\tsame-edge cracks, rectangles, bars, and branching/noisy regions remain grey.\\n   102\\t</description>\\n   103\\t</reference_puzzle>\\n   104\\t\\n   105\\t<reference_puzzle index=\\\"6\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"48634b99\\\" lines=\\\"14-27\\\">\\n   106\\t<description>\\n   107\\tAdvance the marker from one half of a vertical bar to the same half of the next longer bar.\\n   108\\t\\n   109\\tInput structure\\n   110\\t- The grid has one dominant background color and exactly two foreground colors.\\n   111\\t- One foreground color forms many vertical one-cell-wide bars; the other appears as a single vertical marker segment.\\n   112\\t- The marker segment occupies exactly the top or bottom half of its containing vertical bar.\\n   113\\tRule\\n   114\\t- Recolor the current marker segment back to the bar color.\\n   115\\t- Find the unique all-bar-color vertical bar whose height is two pixels greater than the marked source bar.\\n   116\\t- Recolor the same half of that next longer bar to the marker color.\\n   117\\tKey insight\\n   118\\t- Each bar's total height encodes an ordered size, and the marker advances from a 2k bar to the corresponding 2(k+1) bar while preserving whether it marks the top or bottom half.\\n   119\\t</description>\\n   120\\t</reference_puzzle>\\n   121\\t\\n   122\\t<reference_puzzle index=\\\"7\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"fd02da9e\\\" lines=\\\"26-41\\\">\\n   123\\t<description>\\n   124\\tReplace each colored corner marker with its corner-specific inward stencil in the same color.\\n   125\\t\\n   126\\tInput structure\\n   127\\t- The grid is 8x8 with a single dominant background color.\\n   128\\t- Foreground pixels are marker pixels, each located at one of the four corners.\\n   129\\t- A marker's color is carried to the stencil selected by its corner position.\\n   130\\t\\n   131\\tRule\\n   132\\t- Erase each corner marker back to the background.\\n   133\\t- Top corner markers become an inward 2x2 block one cell away from the top and side edges.\\n   134\\t- Bottom corner markers become the mirrored three-pixel inward bent stencil shown by the bottom-corner examples.\\n   135\\t\\n   136\\tKey insight\\n   137\\t- The marker position selects the fixed stencil; the marker color only supplies the paint color, so multiple corners apply independently.\\n   138\\t</description>\\n   139\\t</reference_puzzle>\\n   140\\t\\n   141\\t<reference_puzzle index=\\\"8\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"dd6b8c4b\\\" lines=\\\"9-22\\\">\\n   142\\t<description>\\n   143\\tMove the closest reachable maroon pixels into the 3×3 block around the unique red center.\\n   144\\t\\n   145\\tInput structure:\\n   146\\t- bg = orange floor, magenta walls, scattered maroon (9) pixels.\\n   147\\t- A unique red (2) pixel marks the center of a 3×3 destination block.\\n   148\\t\\n   149\\tRule:\\n   150\\t- Maroon pixels connected to the destination through floor/maroon cells (not blocked by walls) are candidates.\\n   151\\t- Rank candidates by distance to the destination; the closest ones fill the block in row-major order.\\n   152\\t- Moved maroons are erased (replaced with floor color).\\n   153\\t\\n   154\\tKey insight: Wall barriers restrict connectivity — only maroon pixels reachable via flood-fill through the floor qualify, so proximity alone isn't enough.\\n   155\\t</description>\\n   156\\t</reference_puzzle>\\n   157\\t\\n   158\\t<reference_puzzle index=\\\"9\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"4a1cacc2\\\" lines=\\\"8-23\\\">\\n   159\\t<description>\\n   160\\tFill the rectangle from the lone foreground pixel to its nearest grid corner.\\n   161\\t\\n   162\\tInput structure\\n   163\\t- The grid is a uniform background field with exactly one foreground pixel.\\n   164\\t- The foreground pixel's color is the color used for all added pixels.\\n   165\\t\\n   166\\tRule\\n   167\\t- Find the grid corner with the smallest Manhattan distance to the foreground pixel.\\n   168\\t- Recolor every pixel in the inclusive axis-aligned rectangle bounded by that\\n   169\\t  corner and the foreground pixel to the foreground color.\\n   170\\t\\n   171\\tKey insight\\n   172\\t- The single pixel is one corner of the rectangle; the opposite corner is the\\n   173\\t  nearest corner of the whole canvas.\\n   174\\t</description>\\n   175\\t</reference_puzzle>\\n   176\\t\\n   177\\t<reference_puzzle index=\\\"10\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"9f669b64\\\" lines=\\\"26-48\\\">\\n   178\\t<description>\\n   179\\tPush the central solid rectangle to the grid edge, splitting the perpendicular target rectangle around its path.\\n   180\\t\\n   181\\tInput structure\\n   182\\t- The background is the dominant color.\\n   183\\t- There are exactly three monochrome foreground objects arranged on one\\n   184\\t  horizontal or vertical axis.\\n   185\\t- The middle object on that axis is a solid rectangular moving object.\\n   186\\t- One end object is a solid rectangle or bar whose long side is perpendicular\\n   187\\t  to the movement axis; this is the target to split.\\n   188\\t\\n   189\\tRule\\n   190\\t- Move the middle rectangle along the axis toward the target until it is\\n   191\\t  flush with the grid edge in that direction.\\n   192\\t- Clear the original middle rectangle and the original target.\\n   193\\t- Split the target through the moving rectangle's two-cell-wide path and\\n   194\\t  shift the two halves one cell outward perpendicular to the movement.\\n   195\\t- Keep the other end object unchanged.\\n   196\\t\\n   197\\tKey insight\\n   198\\t- The non-target end object acts as a pusher; the central rectangle travels\\n   199\\t  away from it through the perpendicular target, opening a matching gap.\\n   200\\t</description>\\n   201\\t</reference_puzzle>\\n   202\\t\\n   203\\t<reference_puzzle index=\\\"11\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"ac6f9922\\\" lines=\\\"18-40\\\">\\n   204\\t<description>\\n   205\\tSummarize the enclosed table slots by the single object color inside each slot, using the slot background color for empty slots.\\n   206\\t\\n   207\\tInput structure\\n   208\\t- The most common color forms the outer background and all enclosed slot\\n   209\\t  backgrounds.\\n   210\\t- The enclosed background components form a complete rectangular array of\\n   211\\t  slots, ordered by their positions.\\n   212\\t- Each slot contains either no other color or exactly one object color.\\n   213\\t\\n   214\\tRule\\n   215\\t- Find all 4-connected components of the most common color that do not touch\\n   216\\t  the input edge.\\n   217\\t- Sort their bounding boxes into row and column order to define the output\\n   218\\t  table.\\n   219\\t- For each slot, output its unique non-background color if present; otherwise\\n   220\\t  output the background color.\\n   221\\t\\n   222\\tKey insight\\n   223\\t- The large grid is an expanded table: the enclosed background components are\\n   224\\t  the cells, and any colored object drawn inside a cell is that cell's summary\\n   225\\t  value.\\n   226\\t</description>\\n   227\\t</reference_puzzle>\\n   228\\t\\n   229\\t<reference_puzzle index=\\\"12\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"4c7dc4dd\\\" lines=\\\"7-21\\\">\\n   230\\t<description>\\n   231\\tLearn a transformation rule from a training pair of framed sprites, then apply it to a test sprite.\\n   232\\t\\n   233\\tInput structure:\\n   234\\t- Grid contains several colored square frames (hollow borders of a single color).\\n   235\\t- Each frame's interior holds a small pattern sprite; one frame's interior is blank (all black).\\n   236\\t- Two frames form a training pair (their interiors share the same color palette); one remaining frame is the test case.\\n   237\\t\\n   238\\tRule:\\n   239\\t- Identify the training pair by matching interior color sets; the other non-blank frame is the test input.\\n   240\\t- Infer the rule mapping source→destination (e.g. reflection, color inversion, gap filling, endpoint extraction, or checkerboard complement).\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260619_141339_seed174941624_resume_gpt54_xhigh/10_4.log:2791:- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有若干由同一种非黑色颜色（围栏色，例如 Maroon）构成的封闭矩形围栏，每个围栏是单像素宽的矩形环。每个围栏的边上有一个或多个单像素缺口（\"门\"），缺口处的围栏像素缺失，露出黑色背景。围栏内部全为黑色背景（空心）。围栏之间互不接触。另外，每个围栏内部的某个角落处有一个彩色像素（非黑色、非围栏色），该像素的颜色是该围栏的\"射线颜色\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/9/codegen_prompts/4.md:17:  - 网格下方有若干个由 Maroon 像素构成的一像素厚矩形框，每个框内部可能被 Grey 色的水平或垂直分隔线分成 1-5 个子区域。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/9/codegen_prompts/4.md:20:  - 对每个 Maroon 框，数出其内部 Grey 分隔线将框分成的子区域数量 N。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/